                <pb facs="0726" n="628" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg628"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/2652: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Tenney</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-02-07T17:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 7,
                                1920—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received February 7—1
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>32. Referring to the Legation’s telegram January 30, 5 p.m. Interview with the
                    Premier today. Premier states that if he can <pb facs="0727" n="629"
                        xml:id="pg629"/> get an advance from the four power consortium before
                    Chinese New Years Day, he will give Pacific Development Corporation more time
                    for second advance. He prefers to deal with American in wine and tobacco bureau
                    [reorganization] and will refuse all offers by others if only he can tide over
                    temporary difficulties.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Tenney</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
